cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this workshop or its software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "A hands-on OMOP CDM workshop in R"
abstract: >-
  A hands-on workshop in which participants explore a synthetic OMOP Common Data Model dataset
  (synthea-covid19-10k) in R, with CDMConnector, PatientProfiles and OmopSketch, through a learnr tutorial in
  their browser. A facilitator opens the parts of the workshop and releases feedback live. Everything runs in
  containers: one tutorial per participant (ShinyProxy), a plumber api with the state and the answer key, a Shiny
  facilitator app and Caddy for HTTPS.
